label chapter_4_start:
    $ current_chapter = "ch4"
    $ save_name = _("Chapter IV")
    $ shina_stay_points = 0
    $ road_read = 0
    nvl clear

label ch4_prologue:
    scene bg black with slow_dissolve
    play ambience forestamb fadein 2.0 volume 0.7
    play music bgm_pilgrimage_soft fadein 2.5 volume 0.3
    pause 1.0
    show screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.8)
    pause 0.4
    nvl clear

    n2 "The road through Hino Valley was old when the cedars were young."
    nvl clear
    hide screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.5)
    show bg_01 with slow_dissolve
    pause 1.0
    show screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.5) 

    n2 "Their roots had long since pushed through the packed earth at the edges, cracking the stones with the patience of things that knew they would win eventually."
    n2 "Two carts could not pass each other on a good day."
    n2 "That autumn morning was a good day. Barely."

    nvl clear

    n2 "Beside the cart, Hana — younger, rounder, still optimistic about journeys in a way that four years of shrine work hadn't yet corrected and temple boredom relieved — was telling the driver something about her cousin's wedding." 
    n2 "One where the bride had a gown that brought out the color of her eyes, and a groom who had been so nervous, had relied just a bit too heavily on liquid courage. Hana brushed a mischievous bang out of her eye. Her dark hair was pinned back beneath a travel wrap that had been slipping incrementally since the first valley and which she kept nudging back into place with her knuckle without interrupting herself or apparently noticing she was doing it."

    nvl clear

    n2 "The driver, old Kenta, was nodding. Once every few words, a grunt. He was always nodding. Makoto had never been certain how much he actually heard. He rolled his left shoulder. Then his right. Only one rolled smoothly."
    ha2 "—and the lanterns! You should have seen the lanterns, there were so many that you couldn't—"
    ken2 "Mmm…"
    ha2 "— count them all! It was like something out of a painting."
    n2 "The road curved the same way Hana's conversation did. The cedars closed in on both sides, taller here, older. The light thinned. The air smelled of cold earth and something sweet underneath, some plant she had never identified, that grew only in this particular bend of the valley where the drainage collected and the soil stayed damp even in dry weeks."

    nvl clear

    n2 "She had been thinking about the bath at the sister shrine — the wood tub worn dark with use, the weight of hot water after a full day in the saddle — when the first arrow found the driver."

    nvl clear
    hide screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.5)
    show bg_02 with slow_dissolve
    show screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.5)  
    pause 1.0
    n2 "The reins slipped from his hands. The horse shied. The cart lurched."
    n2 "Holding the rear, was the hired guard."
    n2 "Makoto took her eyes off the road in front of her only for a moment and turned. He was still there, still mounted, his face gone white and very still, the kind of still that meant he was deciding. Judging by how neat his clothes were, despite his trade- one could safely assume his choice. His horse shifted under him and he slowly patted its neck, not even looking at Makoto, but past her."
    n2 '"Guard," she said, in a tone that was mixed with both warning and caution. '
    n2 "He looked at her."
    n2 "She had time to see it happen. It was hard to miss. The decision settling in and turning over and over. The color started leaving his face entirely.  "

    n2 "The hired guard turned his horse and rode back the way they had come."
    n2 "The sound of hooves faded into the cedars."
    n2 "Then the road was quiet."
    nvl clear
    hide screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.5)
    jump ch4_s1_road

## S1 — The Road
label ch4_s1_road:
    show bg_03 with dissolve
    pause 1.0
    show screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.5)  
    n2 "Seven men. The procession reduced to its essentials: two attendants who could not run, Makoto herself, and the road."
    n2 "She stepped in front of the cart."
    n2 "Her hands were shaking. She pressed them flat against her thighs."
    n2 "Behind her: the sound of Sato trying to breathe steadily, and failing."
    n2 "Hana- choking through stiffled sobs."
    mk2 "Run."
    n2 "Neither moved."
    n2 "The bandit leader stepped over Kenta's body without looking down."
    ban2 "A priestess? On a horse? That's unusual."
    ban2 "Doesn't matter. Drop the outer robes and afterwards we can consider letting the other two go."
    nvl clear
    pause 0.5
    hide screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.5)
    hide bg_02 with dissolve    

    scene bg black
    pause 0.5
    n2 "He reached for her collar."
    nvl clear
    show bg_02_5 with dissolve
    pause 0.5
    show bg_03 with dissolve
    pause 1.0
    show screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.5) 
    n2 "The woman came out of the treeline without announcing herself."
    n2 "Dark red hair, road-worn clothes, a naginata held easy in one hand. Not quite twenty, with the look of someone the road had been working on since before it should have had her."
    n2 "She didn't look at Makoto. She was already reading the men — their spacing, who was hesitating, who was committed — with the swift, practical attention of someone who had learned that attention was the difference."
    nvl clear
    n2 "She stepped forward."
    pause 0.5
    scene bg black with dissolve
    n2 "What happened after that was efficient and brief. A body that had stopped having to think about it, working through the geometry of the problem."
    n2 "When it was over, a branch settled in the cedars. The last two men were gone."
    nvl clear

    show nvl_shina neutral at nvl_stage_left onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    show nvl_makoto neutral at nvl_stage_right onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    hide screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.5)
    show bg_04 with dissolve
    pause 1.0
    show screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.5)
    sh2 "You."
    sh2 "What were you doing?"
    mk2 "Standing where I was."

    n2 "The young woman stared at her. Her gaze flickered over to the two women behind her, and then back to a direct gaze at Makoto."

    sh2 "Stupid."
    pause 0.6
    sh2 "But I've seen worse reasons to bleed."
    n2 "The woman turned away slightly, rolling her shoulders as she reached into her shirt to pull out a small cloth. She wiped her blade clean without looking at it, and then tucked it back into her shirt."
    n2 "Now that the danger was gone, Makoto could lower her guard just enough to notice the small things about her."

    nvl clear

    $ menu_owner = "makoto"
    menu:

        "The grip. Already at rest.":
            $ road_read += 1
            $ shina_stay_points += 1
            n2 "The naginata was back to easy carry before the last man had finished falling. Her breathing had not changed — or if it had, it had corrected itself before the count was done."
            n2 "Makoto had watched enough people move under real pressure to understand what it meant when a body stopped having to decide."

        "The eyes. Still working.":
            $ road_read += 1
            n2 "Even now, she was not looking at Makoto. She was checking the road. The treeline. The bend where the remaining men had disappeared."
            n2 "Not finished. Still calculating. The problem was not over until the problem was definitively over, and she had apparently decided for herself when that was."

        "The smell of the road on her.":
            n2 "Cedar and cold air and woodsmoke. The particular smell of someone who had been sleeping outdoors long enough that it had settled into the cloth rather than sitting on top of it."
            n2 "Not a shrine guard. Not a court appointment. Someone the road had made from other materials entirely."

    $ menu_owner = None
    nvl clear
    hide nvl_shina neutral onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    hide nvl_makoto neutral onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    nvl clear
    sa2 "Lady, we should move off the road immediately."
    n2 "Interrupting, the woman named her price. Three days' work at a stated rate. Paid on arrival. Meals included. If there was trouble on the road, that was part of the rate."
    n2 "Sato made a sound."
    sa2 "T-that is awfully presumptuous of you. And your price--"
    mk2 "Fair. For the distance and the risk. Yes."
    n2 "The woman turned and began righting the supply cart with the businesslike attention of someone who had already moved on to the next problem."
    nvl clear
    n2 "Even though she had just wiped her naginata clean, she used it as a lever to right the cart."
    sh2 "Cart's salvageable. Lost some of the load when it went over."
    sh2 "Dunno. You'll probably want to check what broke."
    n2 "A pause."
    sh2 "The driver..."
    n2 "There was a moment of heavy silence."
    sh2 "If you have any fabric--"
    n2 "Sato stepped around to the back of the cart. Silently, she lifted the lid of one of the wooden crates."
    sa2 "I can--"
    n2 "The wine-red haired woman took the fabric from Sato. She didn't ask for them. Simply took them."
    nvl clear
    sh2 "I'll be back."
    show forest path with dissolve
    pause 0.5
    n2 "Part of Makoto wanted to watch the woman wrap the stiff body. This absolute stranger seemed to read the situation and took charge accordingly. Neither of the three of them were in any condition to deal with a deceased body."
    n2 "Instead, the priestess silently stood to the side of the cart. A calming presence for the young woman who was again on the verge of fresh tears. "
    n2 "The minutes dragged like hours until there was a heavy thud landing in the back of the cart."
    n2 "Hana remained silent the entire time. Sato moved to sit next to Hana, who's hands were shaking as she white-knuckeled the reins."
    n2 "Sato laid a hand on Hana's shoulder for a brief moment before taking the reins from Hana's grip. Gently."
    n2 "Makoto was already on her mare."
    sh2 "Sun's still high. Probably should keep moving."

    nvl clear
    hide screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.5)
    show bg_05 with dissolve
    pause 1.0
    show screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.5)
    n2 "The woman brushed past the priestess, the smell of oak and campfire, and walked in front."
    n2 "Not far ahead. Close enough to hear trouble before it arrived. But ahead, clearly, with no suggestion the arrangement was open for discussion."
    n2 "The naginata rode across her shoulders in a posture that managed to look simultaneously relaxed and ready."
    n2 "In the first hour, she said nothing."
    n2 "In the first hour, Makoto learned the length of her stride."
    nvl clear

    show nvl_makoto neutral at nvl_stage_right onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    n2 "Sato leaned over just a bit, closer to the priestess before she spoke."
    sa2 "My lady... she has no manners whatsoever."
    mk2 "She saved our lives."
    sa2 "That does not preclude manners."

    sh2 "I can hear you."
    n2 "Makoto rarely saw such a reaction from the older advisor. Sato went rigid."
    sh2 "Sound carries on mountain roads. Especially when it's quiet."
    nvl clear
    pause 0.5
    sh2 "...."
    sh2 "...and I have excellent manners. I haven't even complained about the pace once."
    nvl clear
    hide screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.5)
    scene bg black with dissolve
    pause 0.5
    show screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.5)
    n2 "Makoto looked down at the reins."
    n2 "She brushed a small fraying chip of worn leather on the reins between her fingers."
    n2 "She did not smile."
    n2 "Or tried not to."
    nvl clear
    hide screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.5)
    stop music fadeout 2.0
    stop ambience fadeout 2.0
    pause 2.0
    jump ch4_s2_shrine

## S2 — The Shrine

label ch4_s2_shrine:
    scene bg temple_dusk with slow_dissolve
    play ambience forestamb fadein 2.0 volume 0.6
    play music temple_theme fadein 2.0 volume 0.3
    pause 1.0
    show screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.8)
    pause 0.4
    nvl clear

    n2 "Three days, and Makoto could have told you the exact length of Shina's stride, the way she rolled her left shoulder when the road climbed, how she took her rice — fast, without comment, like eating was a task to be completed."
    n2 "She could not have told you where Shina was from. Or how long she'd been on the road. Or whether anyone was waiting for her somewhere."
    n2 "Every question that reached in that direction met a short answer, or a shrug, or simply silence — offered without hostility, the way someone closes a door without slamming it."
    n2 "Not rude. Just closed."

    nvl clear

    n2 "At the gate of the sister shrine, Makoto watched her face when the kitchen smell reached them properly — rice and miso and something with ginger, warm and specific after a day of cold road and cedar."
    n2 "Something moved through Shina's expression. Fast, involuntary, before her face went back to order."
    n2 "Makoto looked away before she was caught looking."

    nvl clear

    n2 "Before she went inside, Shina stopped at the inner gate."
    n2 "She studied the bracket, the bolt, the warped place in the wood where the latch sat wrong."

    show nvl_shina neutral at nvl_stage_left onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve

    sh2 "Your latch is bad."
    sa2 "I'll have it seen to."
    sh2 "Someone with quiet hands could walk it open and you'd never hear them."
    sa2 "I'll have it seen to."
    sh2 "Sure."

    n2 "She went inside."
    n2 "Sato closed the door behind her with the particular precision of a woman not allowing herself to comment."

    hide nvl_shina neutral onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    nvl clear

    n2 "She found her on the side steps after the arrival supper."
    n2 "Not the main staircase — the narrow ones the attendants used, functional rather than formal. Third step from the bottom. Bowl in her lap."
    n2 "She was eating with full attention. No pretense of casualness — just the focused quiet of someone genuinely hungry who saw no reason to hide it."

    show nvl_shina neutral at nvl_stage_left onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    n2 "She heard Makoto's footsteps and did not look up."
    sh2 "Not following me, are you."
    show nvl_makoto neutral at nvl_stage_right onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    mk2 "These are my steps."

    n2 "A pause. Then Shina shifted slightly on the step — not moving over, exactly. Just acknowledging that there was room."
    n2 "Makoto sat."

    $ duck(level=0.15, delay=0.3)
    n2 "The courtyard below was empty. The gravel pale in the early dusk. From the main hall, the low sound of an evening bell, and then quiet."
    n2 "She arranged her robes for the step, and the hem of her outer sleeve came to rest across the edge of Shina's step rather than her own."
    n2 "She did not correct it."
    $ unduck(level=0.3, delay=2.0)

    nvl clear

    sh2 "Three days. And you learned nothing about me."
    mk2 "No."
    sh2 "Doesn't bother you?"

    $ duck(level=0.2, delay=0.4)
    mk2 "I learned that you check the perimeter before you sleep. I noticed the first night."
    mk2 "That you don't eat until the people you're responsible for have eaten. You were last to supper both evenings."
    mk2 "That you sleep lightly. One of the attendants knocked over a water jar in the dark, the second night. You were outside her door before she'd picked it up."
    $ unduck(level=0.3, delay=1.5)

    n2 "Shina had gone still."

    mk2 "Those seemed like relevant details."
    mk2 "The rest — I expect there are reasons for."

    show nvl_shina scratch_head at nvl_stage_left onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    sh2 "You're strange."
    sh2 "For a priestess."
    show nvl_makoto amused at nvl_stage_right onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    mk2 "So I'm told."

    n2 "She stood, straightened her robes, and went back up the steps."
    n2 "Behind her, she heard Shina pick up the bowl again. And then, just before the passage door closed — a sound. Small. Not quite a laugh."
    n2 "More the kind of exhale that escapes when someone wasn't expecting to be seen and doesn't entirely mind that they were."
    n2 "Makoto let the door close without pausing."

    nvl clear

    hide nvl_shina scratch_head onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    hide nvl_makoto amused onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve

    n2 "The extended offer came the next morning, through Sato, through the open window."
    n2 "Two months' work. Three weeks at the sister shrine. Four days' escort home. Meals and lodging."
    n2 "The same road stretch where the ambush had been. Same risk, now known."

    show nvl_shina neutral at nvl_stage_left onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve

    sh2 "That's a lot of standing around for three weeks."
    pause 0.5
    sh2 "Fine."

    n2 "Like a concession. Like it cost her something."
    n2 "She followed them through the gate."

    hide nvl_shina neutral onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    nvl clear
    hide screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.5)
    stop music fadeout 2.0
    stop ambience fadeout 2.0
    pause 2.0

    jump ch4_s3_month

## S3 — The Month

label ch4_s3_month:
    scene bg temple_dusk with slow_dissolve
    play ambience forestamb fadein 2.0 volume 0.5
    play music bgm_shrine_morning fadein 2.0 volume 0.25
    pause 1.0
    show screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.8)
    pause 0.4
    nvl clear

    n2 "A month was not a long time."
    n2 "It was long enough."

    nvl clear

    n2 "On the third day, Makoto crossed the lower courtyard at midday."
    n2 "Shina was kneeling at the inner gate."
    n2 "She had her belt knife in one hand and the latch plate in the other, working at the bracket where the wood had warped just enough to make the bolt sit wrong. The latch creaked when it opened. It had been creaking for years."

    show nvl_shina neutral at nvl_stage_center onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve

    n2 "No one had asked her to fix it."
    n2 "Her face had the focused quiet of routine. She did not notice Makoto pass."

    nvl clear

    n2 "Makoto continued on through the upper courtyard."
    n2 "She did not say anything about it. Not then, not later. She added it to the list of things she had observed and not commented on."
    n2 "Someone with quiet hands, Shina had said on the first morning, could walk that latch open without the creak."
    n2 "Someone with quiet hands could no longer do that."

    hide nvl_shina neutral onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    nvl clear

    n2 "Later that same week, Makoto came down the main steps in the late afternoon and stopped."
    n2 "The naginata was leaning against the south post of the covered walkway."
    n2 "It had been there since after the morning rites."
    n2 "Shina was nowhere visible."

    nvl clear

    n2 "A ronin who was passing through did not set the weapon down."
    n2 "The weapon was the road. The weapon was leaving."
    n2 "Makoto looked at the south post for a moment."
    n2 "Then she went on to where she had been going."

    nvl clear

    n2 "The rest of the month moved the way months at the shrine moved."
    n2 "The bell. The rites. The slow turn of autumn light."
    n2 "Shina at the wall during the morning rites. Shina at the outer gate when the village families came through. Three paces behind in formal contexts, without anyone having told her."

    nvl clear

    n2 "She heard it in passing, coming around the covered walkway on the east side of the grounds."
    n2 "Two junior attendants, voices low, not looking where their sound was going."

    $ duck(level=0.15, delay=0.3)
    n2 "She did not slow down."
    $ unduck(level=0.25, delay=1.0)

    n2 "'Do you think Lady will finally take a Shadow? She's never had one before, has she?'"
    n2 "'Never. They say she decided against it. After what happened to the last Priestess's guard — you can't blame her, really.'"
    n2 "'All three of them?'"
    n2 "'That's what I heard.'"

    nvl clear

    n2 "The attendants moved on."
    n2 "Their voices dropped into the courtyard noise and disappeared."

    show nvl_shina neutral at nvl_stage_center onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve

    $ duck(level=0.1, delay=0.3)
    n2 "Shina kept walking."
    n2 "She did not stop to ask what she had heard."
    n2 "She did not stop at all."
    $ unduck(level=0.2, delay=2.0)

    nvl clear

    n2 "She filed it the way she filed things — quietly, without comment, below the level where thinking happens."
    n2 "The latch. The naginata against the south post. This."
    n2 "A list she had not known she was keeping."

    hide nvl_shina neutral onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    nvl clear

    $ duck(level=0.15, delay=0.4)
    n2 "Sometimes, walking past the side steps in the early evening, Makoto would hear it again."
    n2 "The same small exhale she had heard the first night. Shina was usually alone, eating, watching the courtyard go dark."
    n2 "Makoto did not stop. She did not look."
    n2 "She kept walking, the way she had kept walking the first time."
    $ unduck(level=0.3, delay=2.0)

    nvl clear

    n2 "Two weeks in, a letter arrived from the Tanaka shrine."
    n2 "Makoto had been reading it twice — once to understand it, once to understand what was beneath it — when she heard the footsteps."

    $ duck(level=0.15, delay=0.3)
    n2 "Her hand paused on the brush."
    n2 "She did not look up."
    $ unduck(level=0.3, delay=1.5)

    show nvl_shina neutral at nvl_stage_left onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    n2 "Shina appeared in the doorway."

    sh2 "What's that one."

    show nvl_makoto neutral at nvl_stage_right onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    mk2 "Correspondence."
    sh2 "From who."
    mk2 "Are you assigned to receiving my mail now."

    show nvl_shina smug at nvl_stage_left onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    sh2 "Just curious who writes in handwriting that bad."

    show nvl_makoto amused at nvl_stage_right onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    mk2 "It's not the handwriting. It's the brush. The Tanaka shrine has been using the same brushes since before the war."
    sh2 "That tracks."
    mk2 "Be polite."
    sh2 "I am extremely polite. I'm asking about handwriting."

    $ duck(level=0.2, delay=0.4)
    n2 "She had set the brush down. Her shoulders had eased. Her sleeve had drifted across the edge of the writing table without her correcting it."
    n2 "She was about to say something else when the second set of footsteps arrived."
    $ unduck(level=0.3, delay=1.5)

    nvl clear

    $ duck(level=0.2, delay=0.3)
    n2 "Different footsteps. Measured. Older."
    n2 "Sato."
    $ unduck(level=0.3, delay=0.8)

    n2 "The change came before the door opened."
    n2 "Makoto's hand returned to the brush. Her sleeve corrected itself. The smile that had been on her face went smaller, more contained, before it left entirely."
    n2 "Her shoulders settled into the carriage she carried in formal contexts — not stiffer, exactly. More arranged. The Priestess returning to the body she occupied."

    show nvl_shina neutral at nvl_stage_left onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    n2 "Shina watched this happen."
    n2 "She did not move."

    nvl clear

    n2 "Sato entered with the slight bow of someone who had been entering this room for eleven years."

    sa2 "My lady. The village headman has sent his weekly accounting."
    sa2 "And Doi would like to confirm the order of the offerings for the autumn rite."

    show nvl_makoto neutral at nvl_stage_right onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    mk2 "The accounting can wait until evening."
    mk2 "Tell Doi I will speak with her after the noon bell."
    sa2 "Yes, my lady."

    n2 "Sato glanced once at Shina in the doorway. A glance that managed to be entirely correct and entirely a comment."
    n2 "Then she bowed and withdrew."

    nvl clear

    $ duck(level=0.12, delay=0.4)
    n2 "The room was quiet again."
    n2 "Shina had not moved from the doorway."
    n2 "Makoto's hand was still on the brush."
    $ unduck(level=0.25, delay=2.0)

    n2 "After a moment, she set it down again."
    n2 "Her shoulders eased — partly, not fully. Her sleeve did not return to where it had been."

    show nvl_makoto amused at nvl_stage_right onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    mk2 "You were saying something about handwriting."

    show nvl_shina neutral at nvl_stage_left onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    n2 "Shina looked at her for a moment that was longer than the moment required."

    sh2 "Was I."
    mk2 "Something insulting, I believe."
    sh2 "Mm."

    n2 "She did not pick the joke back up."
    n2 "She stood in the doorway a beat longer than usual, looking at Makoto without making the look mean anything in particular."
    n2 "Then she pushed off the frame."

    sh2 "I'll be at the south wall."

    n2 "She left."
    n2 "Makoto picked the brush back up."
    n2 "The letter had not changed. The handwriting was still bad."
    n2 "She read the second paragraph three times without taking it in."

    hide nvl_shina neutral onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    hide nvl_makoto amused onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    nvl clear

    n2 "At the end of the third week, Sato found Shina at the south wall."
    n2 "She did not open with the appointment."

    show nvl_shina neutral at nvl_stage_left onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve

    sa2 "You are a disruption to this shrine's order."

    n2 "Shina said nothing. Waiting."

    sa2 "She seems to require the disruption."

    n2 "Sato did not elaborate."
    n2 "She moved immediately into the formal terms of the appointment — the selection right invoked, the court confirmation required, the oath to follow at the home shrine in front of witnesses."
    n2 "Shina would have until the following evening to give her answer."
    n2 "Sato left before she could respond to the first part."

    hide nvl_shina neutral onlayer nvl_chars with dissolve
    nvl clear

    n2 "Shina had not answered by morning."
    n2 "She had not answered by noon."
    n2 "By late afternoon, Makoto in her writing room had set her brush down and not picked it up again."

    $ duck(level=0.1, delay=0.3)
    n2 "From the window she could see the lower courtyard, and the side wall above it, and the maple."
    n2 "She rose."
    $ unduck(level=0.2, delay=2.0)

    nvl clear
    hide screen nvl_frame with Dissolve(0.5)
    stop music fadeout 2.0
    stop ambience fadeout 2.0
    pause 2.0

    jump ch4_s4_night

## S4 — The Night Before

